# Locally computed (2026-09-04) -- upstream publishes NO checksums for this
# release: the ip7z/7zip GitHub release for 26.03 carries no checksum assets
# and no hashes in the release body, and 7-zip.org publishes none either
# (re-checked at bump time). BR2_DOWNLOAD_FORCE_CHECK_HASHES=y in the defconfig
# is what makes this file load-bearing rather than decorative.
#
# This is the SAME upstream tarball package/lzma-sdk pins, and the tarball
# sha256 below is therefore identical to the first line of
# package/lzma-sdk/lzma-sdk.hash BY CONSTRUCTION, not by coincidence. It was
# re-derived here independently rather than copied:
#
#   sha256sum dl/lzma-sdk/7z2603-src.tar.xz
#   9cbde5099c6deb73691b0579063da5827522ccbbcba3f0020fd04e8c8c16c0d4
#
# If the two files ever disagree, one of the two packages has been bumped
# without the other -- see the "SAME UPSTREAM TARBALL" comment in 7zip.mk.
# Verified against:
#   https://github.com/ip7z/7zip/releases/download/26.03/7z2603-src.tar.xz
sha256  9cbde5099c6deb73691b0579063da5827522ccbbcba3f0020fd04e8c8c16c0d4  7z2603-src.tar.xz
# DOC/License.txt -- unlike lzma-sdk, this package DOES compile the CPP/ code
# those terms cover (including CPP/7zip/Compress/Rar*, hence the unRAR
# restriction). See the license comment in 7zip.mk for the per-path chain.
# Byte-identical across 26.02 -> 26.03.
#
# Note this package does NOT list DOC/readme.txt in 7ZIP_LICENSE_FILES, and
# must not: DOC/License.txt is the operative licence for the code 7zip ships.
# (lzma-sdk lists it because the public-domain grant for the C/ files lives
# only there.) That asymmetry is why the 26.03 bump broke lzma-sdk's
# legal-info and not this package's.
sha256  9ac2b4a97ab5d523965534d8b2d5868e511b39096d51fff458ab72c38b80fccc  DOC/License.txt
